# '(' and '[' are one token (open): `X "(" X "["` names the terminal OPEN
# twice. The second hint is a located error of its own, not a hint that
# "has no effect".
# error: x_hint_same_terminal.grammar:21:10:
# error: X "[" on expr → IDENT names OPEN, as X "(" does; write one of them
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    open
    close
    eof
    err
'\n'                                        → skip, skip
'('                                         → open
'['                                         → open
[)\]]                                       → close
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
exprs! = expr+                              → (exprs ...1)
expr   = IDENT X "(" X "["                  → (var 1)
       | IDENT OPEN expr CLOSE              → (call 1 3)
       | OPEN expr CLOSE                    → 2
